            <ArticleTitle>[Hematocolpos : an unappreciated diagnosis of hymen imperforation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>478-481</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The imperforation of the hymen is a relatively rare congenital malformation. It usually manifests itself in adolescence by a hematocolpos. Hematocolpos is the vaginal retention of menstrual blood at puberty. It results clinically in painful amenorrhea and more rarely in a pelvic mass syndrome. The diagnosis is easy, it is primarily clinical. Pelvic ultrasound and nuclear magnetic resonance are the complementary examinations to be performed as a preoperative assessment and to detect any associated genito-urinary malformations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
